arguments, 'new' expressions, casts), excluding primitives/common JDK
boilerplate and the class's own name.
Deviations from standard CBO: name-based rather than usage-based coupling;
does not distinguish inheritance vs association coupling; does not resolve
referenced names to fully-qualified identities (same-simple-name classes in
different packages undercount as one dependency).

lcom4_approx (NOT standard LCOM4)
----------------------------------
Counts connected components in a graph where two methods are linked if they
directly access the same DECLARED field of the class.
Deviations from standard LCOM4: no method-invocation edges; no inherited
fields; no special handling of static fields; no access-through-other-object
modeling.

cc_class / ccn (Cyclomatic Complexity - decision points counted)
--------------------------------------------------------------------
Decision points counted: if / while / do / for / switch-case / catch /
ternary-expression / && / ||. cc_class is computed over the WHOLE class AST;
ccn is the mean per-method complexity. Confirm this decision-point set
matches whatever CC definition is cited as the reference in the paper.

architecture_size (Composite Structural Complexity Index - NOT a validated
single latent construct)
----------------------------------------------------------------------------
Unweighted mean of min-max-normalized loc, num_methods, cbo_approx,
lcom4_approx, total_method_cc, cc_class. LOC, coupling, cohesion, and
complexity are conceptually distinct properties; this composite has not
been construct-validated (e.g. via factor analysis) as measuring one
underlying dimension. Report as 'Composite Structural Complexity Index',
not 'architecture size', unless/until validated.
"""


def write_metric_definitions_doc(project_dir):
    """Write METRIC_DEFINITIONS_DOC to the project's output folder."""
    try:
        path = os.path.join(project_dir, "metric_definitions.txt")
        with open(path, "w", encoding="utf-8") as f:
            f.write(METRIC_DEFINITIONS_DOC)
        logger.info(f"Metric definitions/deviations doc written to '{path}'")
    except Exception as e:
        logger.warning(f"Could not write metric_definitions.txt: {e}")


def main(project_name, code_dir):
    project_dir = os.path.join(EXPORT_DIR, project_name)
    os.makedirs(project_dir, exist_ok=True)
    write_metric_definitions_doc(project_dir)
    metrics_file = os.path.join(project_dir, "code_metrics.pkl")
    logger.info("--- Starting advanced code metrics calculation ---")
    logger.info(f"INFO messages shown here. Warnings and errors logged to '{ERROR_LOG_FILE}'.")
    overall_start_time = time.time()
    if not os.path.isdir(code_dir):
        logger.error(f"Source code directory not found: {code_dir}.")
        logger.info("Program stopped due to missing source directory.")
        return
    cutoff = get_cutoff(project_name)  # raises if no cutoff is configured
    snap = git_snapshot_at(code_dir, cutoff)
    with snap:
        metrics = compute_code_metrics_for_project(code_dir, project_name)
    if metrics:
        try:
            with open(metrics_file, "wb") as f: pickle.dump(metrics, f)
            write_cutoff_marker(project_dir, "metrics", cutoff, snap.commit_hash)
            logger.info(f"Advanced code metrics successfully saved to '{metrics_file}'")
        except Exception as e:
            logger.error(f"Cannot save code metrics to pickle file: {e}")
            logger.info(f"Saving metrics to '{metrics_file}' failed. Check '{ERROR_LOG_FILE}'.")
    else:
        logger.warning("No metrics calculated (likely no processable Java files found). Output file not saved.")
        logger.info("No metrics calculated. Output file not saved.")
    logger.info(f"--- Advanced code metrics calculation completed in {time.time() - overall_start_time:.2f} seconds ---")
    logger.info(f"Check '{ERROR_LOG_FILE}' for warnings or errors.")


